Allan,

Give Jim Craig @ Data Security of Lincoln, NE a call at (800) 225-7554.

Data Security offers a number of degaussers, rated Type 1, 2, 2a, and
soon type 3.  Without going into a lot of detail (Jim will do this),
DLT is a high coecervity (hope I got that spelled correctly), I think
greater than 1500 oersteds.  In this case, the residual signal cannot
be brought down to a acceptable level to be considered "erased" by 
industrial security standards, but enough for the drive to find it
blank and unformatted when accessed.  Their units have special adapters
for holding the media (TKxx in your case); you can purchase the ones 
you need.

Jim is a good guy, appears to know his stuff, and will give you all the
details you want and then some.

Hope this helps...

Kevin Reynolds



