The "DEC 5900," "DEC 5240" and "DEC 5200" are all the same chassis with
different configurations

The DECsystem 5900 is a rack-mount version that was typically sold as a
server in a 19" rack with disks and the like.  It had a (I think) 33Mhz
R3000A processor in it.

The DECstation 5000-240 and DECstation 5000-200 are workstations.  The
240 is a R4000 based system, I can't remember the speed. The 200 is an
R3000A based system at 33Mhz.

The DECstation 5000-33 and 5000-20 are the low-end desktop system, both
based on the R3000A.  One is 33Mhz, one is 20Mhz.  


All of these systems are upgradeable to R4000 processors (except of
course, the 240 which already is an R4000) so you may or may not have
them.  The difference between the packages comes in TURBOchannel slots,
memory (parity vs ECC and capacity) and internal storage capacity.  (as
well as general system performance)


Hope that helps

Bill Jackson




