In article <DAuCFC.5r8@festival.ed.ac.uk>, jlothian@castle.ed.ac.uk (J Lothian) writes:
> Everything is currently on an RA81. However, I also
> have a 1Gb SMD disk attached to an emulex UD33 
> controller which I would like to use. However, at the
> moment, the controller identifies the disk as an RA81,
> which means that the BSD uda driver uses the RA81 
> partitions for it (this is an *old* version of 4.3).
> I need to be able to persuade the 
> controller to identify the drive as something else, so 
> that I can add a new partition table to the driver. 

  As far as I recall, everything is an RA81 to a UD33. It's unlikely that
any DEC disk has the same capacity as your disk, so you'd either be too
small or wasting space, depending on which way the error went.

  I would suggest editing the driver source to deal with your new drive.
Of course, that will mis-size your existing RA81, but if you added new
partitions starting where your RA81 ends, you could just not use them on
the real RA81.

  Or you could get a newer release that supports disk labeling (that was
certainly present by 4.3/Reno.

