From: aaron@garply.com (Aaron Sakovich)
Subject: Re: Which one run FASTER!? F77 on OSF/1 or WinNT.
Date: 1995/06/28
Message-ID: <3sqluc$30e@acara.snsnet.net>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 105128771
references: <3sl20i$c6@akiu.gw.tohoku.ac.jp>
organization: Net Results
reply-to: aaron@garply.com
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

>If I have two Alpha Station with same CPU.
>But, One run on OSF/1 3.2 and one on WindowsNT3.5.
>How mach will the speed differ between a similar program of F77.

If it's 32 bit code, there probably won't be much difference.  With
64 bit code, the edge goes to OSF/1.  If it were C, I'd say OSF/1
regardless, as Digital has control over the compiler and can tune it
for the platform.  VC++ is MS's, and Digital can't tweak it for
performance directly.  There is the axp_dpml for NT, but there's more
of that for Digital UNIX.

How much of a delta is code specific -- I can only speculate as to which
is faster.

Aaron

