In article <3sb1q1$oqg@news.uni-c.dk>, "S�ren Granfeldt" <sgaci@inet.uni-c.dk> writes:
> Hi, I'm running Pathworks 4.2 on a VAX/VMS 5.5-2 server;
> 
> Sometimes my user are unable to log in using PCSA/Pathworks 5.0 
> 
> When they try to use their private service such as \\VAX1\MYNAME
> the server rejects their password and they're refused even though the 
> password is correct and there is nothing wrong with thier account;
> 
> Has anyone experienced the same problem and found a solution ?

Yes.

We have had at least two things give these symptoms:

1.  Client PC has run out of re-directions.  Default is 8.  If you are using
    Windows, try USE command from DOS.  The error messages are better.
    Solution: If this is the problem, get user to reduce number of redirections
    used or increase the limit.

2.  Bug in PW 4 server.  (Fixed in V5, supposedly).  After someone gets these
    errors, try "$ SHOW INTRUSION" on the server.  If the user shows up in
    the intrusion list, you probably have this problem.
    Work-around:  increase these SYSGEN parameters:
	LGI_HID_TIM=5
	LGI_BRK_LIM=10
    This will, however, reduce the security on your system.

