In article <DAH2FM.Cuw@actrix.gen.nz>,
Allan Lawrie <madpunk@atlantis.actrix.gen.nz> wrote:
>Well, ive got one of these beasts and 1.3GB of storage. It boots
>ok but there's one wee problem. The console port accepts NO data
>from the terminal. I have checked the connector (DB25), it uses
>pins 1, 2, 3 & 24. The 24 puzzles me, is it something important?

Are you seeing the initial Micro Verify Test output (couple of %%)? If 
not, have you got the right baud rate (see Backpanel decal)? If you have 
console prompt >>>, is the Console Keyswitch in Local position? What's 
happening with the CPU State LEDS (be careful the Error Light glows when 
everything is normal)? Somebody who knows can tell me about the 'Logic' of 
the error lamp glowing when everything is OK. If no characters sent to 
terminal and everything else looks dead, check the power controller 
status (down bottom on rear left hand side of processor cabinet). Does 
the terminal you use have appropriate links to work with only pins 1, 2 & 
3 on RS-232 connector. Be careful, the terminal may spit the dummy if it 
is not seeing appropriate RS-232 status via links on its connector.

Hopefully this gives you something to start with. Please post back here
with answers and CC to my EMail Address. I can't guarantee I'll read your
message in a reasonable time as I'm not getting onto local service
provider that often. 
   
Regards,
Garry Page

gpage@melbpc.org.au



