We are running Progress on a DEC Alpha platform using OpenVMS as the
operating system.  Last year we had many problems with database crashes
and other problems.  Progress has stated at last year's Progress User's
Conference that no additional resources would be put in place to 
address these problems as OpenVMS is only 10% of their business.  They
also stated that since DEC OSF/1 was a 64-bit O/S it would receive the
same or less priority as OpenVMS because they didn't have a lot of 
customers running on OSF/1 (now called Digital UNIX).  The current 
version of Progress for OpenVMS/Alpha is 6.2N10, while 7.x has been 
released on other O/S's for over a year.

If I were you I would ask my Progress salesman for 2 or 3 customers
running Progress on each O/S you are considering.  Talk to people who
are already running Progress on the O/S in question.  Maybe some 
priorities have changed at Progress.

