utech@rummelplatz.uni-mannheim.de (Utech) writes: 
>
>HELP!
>
>I've got a DEC RZ24 SCSI disk without any manual papers. I want to
connect
>it to my PC over ADAPTEC-2842 SCSI Controller. When I try to format
the disk
>over the ADAPTEC low level formating menu, folowing message appears:
>
>             Unexpected SCSI Command Failure
>
>   Target SCSI ID               2
>   SCSI CDB Sent                03 00 00 00 0E 00
>   Host Adapter Status  00h - No host adapter error
>   Target status                02h - Check condition
>   Sense Key            02h - Not ready
>   +Sense Code          04h
>   +Sense Code Qualifier        00h
>
>Can somebody tell me what is wrong. Do I need to change some jumper
settings
>on the disk. I've found the jumpers to change the SCSI-ID, but without
any
>documentation I can go further ...
>
>Thanks ...
>

DEC RZxx disks that were originally installed in workstations do not
"spin up" on power-on.  (disks that came in PC's do spin up)  

The RZ22, RZ23, RZ24, RZ55 and RZ56 don't have a jumper to enable
spinup, all other RZxx disks do and you should find it in your users
manual.  As for the ones that don't have a jumper, there is a software
"bit" that enables spin-up on power-on.  There are many ways to set
this bit (and I think Kenny House of DEC has posted a FAQ here about
how to do it) but if you know anyone who has a Macintosh with
SilverLining, that's the easiest way to set the spinup bit.  


-bill




