>In message <1995Jun22.094654.4970@nomina.lu.se>, nn said:
>  >  
>  > I opened the external HD:Rz55-F3 and found some strange things... 
>  >  
>  > Connected to the powersupply there is a strange card with lots of
>  > resitors, with absolutely NO function ! 
>  >  
>  > Can someone tell me why they are there ?
>  
>    This may be the 'load module', which puts a load in addition to
>   that of the disk drive on the power supply, which as I understand
it
>   is the same as that which is used in the uVAX2000, the load module
>   simulating the load of the uVAX2000 CPU module.
>    
>   Best Regards,
>   Brian
>   
>   brobson@cix.compulink.co.uk
>   
>
Right, the load  module is in the boxes that were modified VAXstation
2000's so that the power supplies will regulate properly.    Power
supplies are designed with a certain load in mind, and will only
regulate properly when the load is within specified limits.  The RZ55
(AND TZ30 for that matter) don't draw enough current for the power
supply to regulate properly, so a load-board is installed.  It's
substantially cheaper than redesigning the power supply.  

-bill



