No difference.  DEC standard monitor designations are 

    VRxxx-xA     120V, Northern Hemisphere
    VRxxx-x3     240V, Northern Hemisphere
    VRxxx-x4     240V, Southern Hemisphere.


Now, of course on monochrome monitors, there is no northern and
southern, so one has to choose if they pick -x3 or -x4 for the 240V
variant.   Looks like this one is the -x4.  (I've seen them both ways)


BTW, the VRM17 is  a 17" multisync monochrome monitor with maximum
resolution of 1280x1024 at 72Hz.  It was used on the VAXstation 4000
family (VLC, Model 60, Model 90) and on the Personal DECstation 5000
family.  I don't believe that this monitor was ever qualified on the
Alpha families, but could be wrong on that one.  Certainly not on the
Model 400 through 900, maybe on the Model 300 series.  

-bill



