John you did not mention the model number of the Seagate drive,  I am
not aware of a current production 6GB Seagate, but DIGITAL SCSI-2
drivers do not really like Seagate drives, especially Barracudas. 
OpenVMS v6.1 and v6.2 have patches to allow the drivers to work, and
therefore the drives with the current Seagate SCSI-2 drives.  Most of
the time...<G>

I would try one drive if you can before investing in it.  Connect the
drive and do an INIT and then MOUNT/FOR in order to BACKUP/IMAGE
another drive to it.  That should do enough testing of the driver.

If it works, it works!  Otherwise...  DIGITAL may have v5.5-2 SCSI-2
drivers which would help.

Later...




