phdewi@swcp.com (Phillip Williams) writes:

>I am having a problem with my cluster. I have  4 VAXs II 3 2000s and
>a 3100. All are at VMS 5.1 with DECnet 5.0. The problem is the 3100
>will not join the cluster. I keep getting unable to locate SYSLOA42D.exe
>but when I boot the 3100 and do a dir the file is clearly there. Also
>the 3100 will try to boot off of ESA0 but it looks like its in a loop.

My guess is that when booting into the cluster, you are booting from the disk
of oe of the other systems. Probably this disk lacks the required file and,
since the SYSLOA files are added to new releases of VMS as new hardware is
released, probably hte version of VMS on the disk accessed during the cluster
boot is too old to support the 3100.

Try WRITE SYS$OUTPUT F$GETSYI("VERSION") on both the cluster and the
stand-alone 3100 and see if the versions are an exact match. I suspect one (on
the stand-alone 3100) may be a maint. release that added 3100 support.

