names have 6 characters with a 3 character extension, there is a protection 
code (typically <157>), a creation date (one such was 05-Nov-76), a version 
(usually blank), and an owner ([10023,511]).  [This directory was created on 
12-Sep-86).

     I can physically read the tapes just fine.  When the listing says the 
file size is 3, I generally see a record of 3 blocks, the first two being 640 
bytes, the last being smaller.  I'm trying to figure out how the data are 
placed on the tape, so I might have some hope of decoding the information.

