Thanks to "Steve Thompson <olin@cheme.cornell.edu>" my 9GB disk is now up
and running.  All I needed to do was

    disklabel -wr rrz3c junk

to create the disk label (since "junk" is not in /etc/disktab, "disklabel"
read the drive geometry and used that information to create a large 
partition.

    newfs /dev/rz3c

to create the inodes for the filesystem.

