In article <gchapman-1306952120050001@ts1-10.icis.on.ca> Greg Chapman,
gchapman@icis.on.ca writes:
>If anyone can get me some macro (assembly) code on the MicroVax, to scan
>for a key press (it'll be linked as an object to a pascal program)... I'd
>be very grateful...
>
Should not need to use Macro.
Check out  SYS$QIOW  with IO$_SENSEMODE ored with IO$M_TYPEAHEADCOUNT.
The function will return you (via pointer in p7) the number of keypress
in the buffer and also inform you of the first character therein (if any)
- It does *not* read that character until you call  SYS$QIOW with
IO$_READxxxx



