newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <1995Jun19.194053.6261@cs.rit.edu>, msn8626@cs.rit.edu
(Michael S Neary) writes:

:Can someone please give me the console commands to tell my MicroVax II to
:boot automatically from DUA0: in the event of a power outage. (Yes, I am 
:going to put it on a UPS but still...). Thanks.

  Assuming the target OpenVMS system root is located in SYS0 and there are
  no other SYS0 roots on the other disks, flip the paddle switch located on
  the console bulkhead -- this bulkhead also contains the console serial
  port connector, the console baud rate selector, and the count-down LED.

  The paddle is labeled with the halt symbol (triangle-in-circle icon), and
  the positions are labeled with the dot-in-circle and dot-not-in-circle
  icons -- the former position means that a console <BREAK> will halt the
  system, and that the system will stop at >>> when powered up.  The latter
  position indicates that <BREAK> is disabled, and that the system will
  auto-boot on power-up.  (The icons are an international labeling standard.
  Personally I prefer the language-specific stickers.)

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
