..Dual Hosting..., well, clustering is what you are looking at!

However, clustering is mainly considered if you want to increase the availability of your 
system. There are probably many better options to increase performance than clustering.

Having said this, of course, if you have many users logging in to these systems you can gain 
performance wise because the VAXcluster software will balance the workload (at login time).

But in general I wouldn't expect too much, especially if you have performance issues on both 
nodes. For the money you'd spend on the Cluster licenses and probably extra licenses of 
existing software you can probably get some interesting packages that help to make better use 
of your resources.

You need to find out where you performance 'problem' lies.

Is it IO, is it Memory, is it CPU ???

Chances are, packages like DECps, IOExpress, MemoryMaster etc. are the answer to your 
performance problem.

hope that helps

