<100603.540@compuserve.com> writes:
 
>Can anyone advise me on the best memory manager for DOS. With EMM386 we are down to 
>450k on some of our laptops. Qemm is not liked by Pathworks. This is a continuing problem, 
>and my users are beginning to get upset about the slowness of apps.
 
Memory management with Pathworks is an art not a science.
 
As far as I know, the amount of free DOS memory has no affect on the speed
of applications.  If you don't have enough DOS memory free some applications
will not run or will stop running if you use certain features of the programs
that require more memory.
 
In general I have found QEMM to be the best memory manager for Pathworks,
however this may be the case for the PC's, Ehternet boards, Pathworks
version that I use.  You must give more information about the version of
DOS, Pathworks, Intel processor and what type of Ethernet connection (board)
you are using.  I have found that later versions of QEMM are always better
then earlier versions.



