In article <3ragst$e9c@news.easynet.co.uk>, carphone@easynet.co.uk (carphone warehouse) writes:
>Can anyone help me and tell me if it is possible to send a NULL
>character to the local printer on a VTxxx terminal ?
>
>It's driving me mad !!!!

Matt --

There are three ASCII codes that you cannot pass: NULL, XON, and XOFF.
Makes printing graphics difficult on many printers, since they make
heavy use of NULL!

To get around this, you can purchase a PostScript printer. If you were
so inclined, you could probably also modify the firmware in the VT
terminal.

