given in the README file, for "Loading" the /dev/none driver. 

------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 3: Update the Loadable Subsystem Database

Update the loadable subsystem database for the /dev/none driver:

        cd /usr/examples/devdriver/none100
        sysconfigdb -a -f stanza.loadable none

This registers the /dev/none device driver with the configuration
management database /etc/sysconfigtab.

------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 4: Configure the /dev/none Driver into the System

Configure the /dev/none driver into the system:

        sysconfig -c none

The sysconfig utility finds the none.mod file in the /subsys
directory.  It then executes the none.mth method to
preconfigure the device driver. Then sysconfig requests that

