In article <3riatp$vv@aed.AED-Graphics.DE>, siggy@aed.aed-graphics.de (Siggy Hensel) writes:
|>
|>Why is an automatic mail to Digital Equipment
|>generated, when I install the DECladebug Software on
|>Digital Unix (OSF/1) ?
|>
|>The mail looks like this:
|>
|>| From: <root@host>
|>| Message-Id: <9503080000.AA00000@host>
|>| Subject: Installed: BASE 3.0-16 on OSF1 host.domain.DE V3.2 214 alpha
|>| Apparently-To: ladebuginstall@zko.dec.com
|>
|>-- 

Siggy,

   We put the mail mechanism into our kit during one of our earlier
internal field tests, so we could track who'd installed DECladebug.
That way, we could insure that it was getting enough testing, in order
to insure a quality product at release.

   Unfortunately, we forgot to remove the mail mechanism from the kit
when it came time to release the kit to the rest of the world.  Color
our faces red. :-)

   The mail mechanism has been removed from kits we've released in the 
meantime.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Jeff Diewald			EASYNET:   VIRRUS::DIEWALD
	DECladebug group		INTERNET:  diewald@virrus.zko.dec.com
	Digital Equipment Corp.

Note: I don't read every article in this group.  If you have debugger 
questions, I may be able to get you an answer.  You're much more likely to 
get an answer if you put "DECladebug" somewhere in your subject line.



