In article <DA4JJq.Ks@cup.hp.com>, Paul Chan <pc@cup.hp.com> wrote:
>I need information of how to migrate from DEC stations and VAXes to the new
>Alpha OSF1 and OpenVAX systems.  Do I need to recompile and relink everything?
>Can I move the executables over and expect it to run?  If I don't have the 
>source files any more, can I move object files (.o files (.o) and link them 
>with native libraries and object files?
When migrating from VAX/VMS to Alpha/VMS, or when migrating from
DECstation Ultrix to Alpha OSF/1 (Digital Unix), DEC provides tools which
can usually translate an executable to be something usable on the target
machine.  The VMS tool is/was called VEST, and the Unix tool is/was called
DECmigrate.  There is no way to migrate executables from a VMS system to
a Unix-ish system, and there is no way to migrate executables from a
Unix-ish system to a VMS system.  DEC offers a migration guide for moving
from VMS to DEC OSF/1 at the source code level.  Our company is in the
business of providing solutions in that arena.  I hope this helps.
--
 Jim Reiss (jim@accelr8.com)    Accelr8 Technology, Denver, Colorado, USA



