In article <3r9p1l$ptg@manquehue.scc.puc.cl>, patricio@huara.ing.puc.cl (Patricio Andres Rodriguez Valdes(VP)) writes:

:Does anyone knows which is the software or how to use the audio port provided
: by the DEC ALPHA 3000-300L?????

  Yes, we [Digital] know of some software that uses the audio port. 
  Which operating system (NT, OpenVMS, UNIX) were you considering?

:Can I use it as a modem???

  No -- it is a bidirectional audio port, not a telephone communications
  (modem) port.   (The audio port can certainly be used for communications,
  but if you're asking this particular question, you probably don't want
  to have to implement -- much less have to listen to -- your own office
  "local area audible tone network." :-)

  You may be interested in using the ISDN port, if ISDN is available in
  your area -- check with your local PTT *before* connecting.  (X.21bis;
  V.24/V.28; ISO 2110, BS.6623:part1, 1985; rates from 2400 to 19,200 bps)
  If not, you will want to use an external modem on the RS232 serial port.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
