carphone@easynet.co.uk (carphone warehouse) wrote:
> Can anyone help me and tell me if it is possible to send a NULL
> character to the local printer on a VTxxx terminal ?
> It's driving me mad !!!!

I ran into this problem a few years ago when trying to print
VAX WordPerfect through a DEC terminal onto an attached printer.
The @$!#!$#%$ terminal just won't pass null characters on to
the printer, so if you're using ESC codes to control the printer
(like most WordPerfect printer drivers do), then the suppression
of nulls will screw up the formatting.  I looked hard for a
VT terminal setting that would prevent this behaviour, but
unfortunately there is no such setting.

The solution I recommended in this particular case is to run
a separate serial line to the printer, and create a VMS print
queue for it.  I don't know if this is appropriate for your
situation.

Another solution that might work (although I haven't tried
it myself) is to use a PC with terminal emulation software
instead of a terminal.  The emulator might allow you to
pass nulls on to the printer.  This is a non-issue at my
present job, because we use WordPerfect for Windows now
anyway, and now we only need to print plain ASCII from the VAX.



