You are missing the fonts.  Furthermore, Answerbook uses the Display
PostScript extension to X.  The fonts need to be copied from a
sparcstation to the DECstation, and their location added to your
decstation fontpath.  See xset doc for how to change fontpath.

Once you have the fonts, you can at least use AnswerBook to save pages
that can later be printed on a PostScript printer.  You can't read the
display without the DPS extension, however.

If you (or anyone else) figure out how to use DPS on a DECstation, let
us know.  I'm still working on it part time, but I'm not feeling real
optomistic, and I have other things I have to do.

In fact, I asked about this last week in comp.unix.ultrix, and there
have been no other responses yet.

