In article <3pt2p2$hb7@senator-bedfellow.MIT.EDU>, gstevens@musenet.org (Glenn Stevens) writes...
>   I was wondering if anyone out there might have some information on a
>Digital LCP01 color inkjet printer? Specificaly, where can one get ink
>cartdridges for it, and what it needs for drivers?

The LCP01 (later renamed LCG01) is a Tektronics 4692 engine with a DEC
processor plugged inside so it can understand DEC ANSI w/color sixels,  ReGIS,
NAPLPS, and GIDIS. (This was '85 or '86 so it was set up to work  with VMS, the
PRO, and the like.) Tek might be a good source for supplies if Digital isn't
selling them anymore--I've got no clear answer either way but I did find a part
number for cyan ink. :-} You don't say what you want to drive it so it's hard
to answer the last part of your question but I know there are no Windows
drivers, for instance. (Hmmm...an LJ250 driver *might* work but
device-dependence being what it is you might not get anything useful.) 
