In article <3r6qsp$7a6@ankh.iia.org>, smselick@ios.com (Steven Selick) writes:
>Hello. Is it possible to send X display info from a unix machine to a 
>Vaxstation 3100? They are networked together.

Yes.

On the Ultrix system, I have a script "create_pt9113_term" that looks like:

dxterm  -display pt9113:0 \
        -ls \
        -geometry 80x38+160+240 \
        -customization "DXterm.title:`hostname` via X"\
        -customization "DXterm.iconName:`hostname` via X" &

Then, I have a DCL symbol on PT9113 that looks like:

  XED8200 == "RSH ED8200 CREATE_PT9113_TERM"

Of course, I have an entry in my .rhosts file that permits this type of access,
and the security on the VAXstation allows access by anyone, anywhere.

So, if I'm on my VAXstation, and I want a session on ed8200, I just type:

	$ xed8200

and about 5 seconds later, a DECterm appears.

