In article <lukem.802414571@huon>, 
lukem@melb.cpr.itg.telecom.com.au (Luke Mewburn) writes...

>Does anyone know the jumper on an RZ25 to set to get the drive to spin
>up on power on?

    Jumper 2 on the J6 connector is IN to spin up on command, OUT to
    automatically spin up.  The note I have indicates that jumpers 5, 7,
    and 8 are always present.

           front of drive
    ,---------------------------.
    |                           |
    - \                         |             jumpers
    -  \J6                      |         1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
    -  /                        |        ,---------------.
    - /                         |        |. . . . . . . .|  J6
    |                           | front  |. . . . . . . .| 
    |                           | of   ========================
    |                           | drive
    |                           |
    |                           |
    |                           |
    |                           |
    |          J4(SCSI)         |
    | _________^__________      |
    |/                    \     |
    `||||||||||||||||||||||-||||'
                            \__/
                             J3(power)

