In article <tylczak.277.2FD4FB0B@alrc.usbm.gov>, tylczak@alrc.usbm.gov writes:
>Hi:
>
>MON-F-TRAP to 10 005172 
>errors in it's startup.  In addition it gives a 
>MON-F-TRAP to 10 026062 
>error with I try to start up BASIC, it has BASIC-11/RT-11 v02.035.

A TRAP to 10 is a reserved instruction trap.  The processor fetched a word from
memory that was to be used as an instruction, and the word is not a valid
opcode.

Why?  Don't know.  Maybe the disk is corrupted so that files that should
contain valid programs now contain something else.

