john derbyshire (john@acmenet.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: Ok as noboddy seems to want to talk about repairing these old PSU's,
: perhaps someone has some old ones that they want to sell.

: I'd love to get my VAX11/780-5 running , but without power is just scrap
: iron

The power supplies are simple 5V 100A and 5V 50A & +/-12 V ~10 A supplies,
configured to run off single-phase 120 V AC, with a US power plug on the
supply.  They produce a power-fail signal, also.  The supplies indicate what
the output is in terms of voltage and current.  They should be easy to 
replace with standard switching supplies.  The cooling blowers suck through
the power supply, so any replacement shouldn't block the flow too much or
allow air to leak in.  In other words, just gut the bad supply and install
a packaged switcher.




