new Toshiba notebook, and had hoped to use an IBM Ethernet Credit Card
adapter, which in theory should be more convenient, faster, etc., than
the Xircom.

After many fits and starts (which included locating newer IBM ECC drivers
on the IBM ftp site, and figuring out more or less how to set them up), I
finally hit a brick wall when it came to loading the appropriate stack for
Pathworks/DECNet itself.  After successfully loading the drivers, it appears
that Pathworks wants to load its scheduler, at which point we learn that the
adapter can't be seen (the message received indicates that the NDIS DLL may
be "broken").

