Message-ID: <3qq4o8$2sk@jac.zko.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 103745512
distribution: world
references: <main.2.0471F2E7@maininc.org>
organization: Digital Equipment Corp
reply-to: hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com (Stephen Hoffman)
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <main.2.0471F2E7@maininc.org>, main@maininc.org
(Main Coordination Center) writes:

:We will be upgrading from 5.5 to 6.X.  I have been told that if you go to 
:6.2 you HAVE to go to DECnet phase V.  I have not been able to confirm this.

  False.  Out of the box, OpenVMS V6.2 runs Phase IV.

  One can certainly upgrade to DECnet OSI -- with DECnet OSI and with the
  integrated-IP support added in OpenVMS V6.2, one can run DECnet over
  transports such as DDCMP, OSI and (with an IP package) IP, and (with an
  IP package that supports the OpenVMS V6.2 integrated IP interfaces) one
  can also issue COPY/FTP, SET HOST/TELNET and other similar integrated-IP
  commands.  And DECnet OSI can interoperate with an existing DECnet Phase
  IV network.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
