X-Deja-AN: 103745513
distribution: world
references: <3qnte7$1mu@kimble.mistral.co.uk>
organization: Digital Equipment Corp
reply-to: hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com (Stephen Hoffman)
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <3qnte7$1mu@kimble.mistral.co.uk>, kimble@mistral.co.uk
(Mark Sheppard) writes:

:I have a couple of old DECserver 200/MCs but no documentation.  I have looked
:at DEC's WWW page to no avail -- all they had was stuff about the newer
:DECserver 90L+.  Eventually I plan to connect them to a Unix (Linux) box and
:hang some dumb terminals off them.  If I'm right in assuming that they use
:DECNET rather than TCP/IP then I'll need some extra software, but that can
:wait.  What I really need right now is documentation, preferably the original
:manuals.  Can anyone point me in the right direction?  On-line stuff, second
:hand manuals, old manuals straight from DEC?

  DECserver 200/MC (terminal servers with modem control) require an
  image be downloaded (via a DECnet-related maintenance protocol called
  MOP), and communications with the host are via the LAT protocol.  To
  my knowledge, there is no IP package nor a DECnet package for these
  DECserver 200-series terminal servers.

  Various newer DECservers do not require the download, and the newer
  DECservers also support protocols in addition to LAT.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------




