is not uncommon for DEC to use a small (<1A) _linear_ supply to power the 
switching oscillator and control circuits, rather than a kick-start 
circuit from the switching supply. This was certainly done in the H7140 
(PDP11/44 supply). The typical output of this transformer is about 12V - 
it is rectified and smoothes and then linked to the input of a 78xx 
series regulator.

