correct, there is no IP package for the 200MC.  The load software is on 
the condist CDs, and to the best of my knowlege (having just 
installed it last week) there is no PAK necessary for the load 
software.  All the install does is to do the correct NCP defines, 
load the DSCONFIG program, and the image for the 200MC.  The license 
to use the software came with the DECserver itself, I believe.  If 
you are trying to do this from LINUX, you are in for a real 
programming chore, and might be better off just getting a multiport 
board (digital, etc) for your LINUX system. Is there a LAT implementation 
for LINUX?  If not, you are out of luck, technically, since LAT is 
licensed by Digital.  Even if it was not licensed, there are a lot of 
people out there that have tried to reingineer the LAT protocol, and failed.

If your DECservers work, and you want to sell them, give me a call and 
maybe I'll buy them from you, and you can use the money to get a 90L or 
compatible from BlackBox (if LINUX supports LAT).

-reed


