re 1, POSIX comes with OpenVMS (which is why the O-P-E-N in OpenVMS 
really isn't all that silent).  So long as the target 
systems are running a recent OpemVMS, they will have 
POSIX.  However, they might not have installed it, which 
means that your installation procedure needs to take that 
into account and install POSIX if necessary.  In general, 
DEC has taken a dim view, mostly for support reasons, of 
software distributors shipping their products with copies 
of VMS images, even if those images are (theoretically) 
already on every openvms system in the universe.

-reed

