The ZLXp-E* series is same the ZLX-E* series for the TurboChannel based 
machines.  They use the same graphics accelerator, the only major difference
is the bus interface.  The ZLXp-E* series, if you look at triangle performance
is an entry level card.  The extra hardware is not in the chip to speed up
shaded triangle, therefore giving you a less costly option.  However, the 
ZLXp-E are very good at 2D and line operations.  The option does all the 
pixel banging and the Alpha does all the calculations.

If you are looking to replace a ZLX-M* or ZLX-L*, then I would suggest that
you talk to your sales person.  There is specific program in place to address
your needs.




